# Everything here is excluded from the Docker build context for ALL services
# (ml-service, api, frontend all use `context: .`). Keeping the context small
# is the single biggest win for build speed — the daemon tars and uploads the
# whole context on every build, even for one-line source changes.

# Python virtualenv — ~5 GB of CUDA/torch wheels, rebuilt inside the image via uv.
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/

# Locally compiled binaries — the image builds its own; a host binary (esp. a
# Windows .exe) is useless in a Linux container and busts the Go build cache.
**/*.exe
api/api
**/*.test

# Node — installed inside the image via `npm ci`.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.vite/

# Runtime data and model weights — mounted as volumes, never baked in.
ml-service/data/
ml-service/models/

# VCS / editor / OS noise
.git/
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
**/*.log

# Docs and local tooling not needed to build any image
docs/
*.md
.env
.env.*
**/.claude/
**/.rsk/
